      <description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;//localhost:1313/wp-content/uploads/2014/04/postcard-2014-20140425_18040268_0104.jpg&#34;&gt;&lt;img alt=&#34;postcard-2014-20140425_18040268_0104&#34; loading=&#34;lazy&#34; src=&#34;//localhost:1313/wp-content/uploads/2014/04/postcard-2014-20140425_18040268_0104.jpg&#34;&gt;&lt;/a&gt; &lt;a href=&#34;//localhost:1313/wp-content/uploads/2014/04/postcard-2014-20140425_18041665_0105.jpg&#34;&gt;&lt;img alt=&#34;postcard-2014-20140425_18041665_0105&#34; loading=&#34;lazy&#34; src=&#34;//localhost:1313/wp-content/uploads/2014/04/postcard-2014-20140425_18041665_0105.jpg&#34;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;From: Freeda C., To: Ruby Chandler&lt;br&gt;
Mailed From: Milford, Illinois on July 24, 1911&lt;br&gt;
Picture Info: Public School, Milford, Ill. Pub. by C.C. Campbell&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Ruby Chandler&lt;br&gt;
Pearl, Illinois&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Well, I’m home. But I sure was tired when I arrived here. But I am well rested up today. Did Marie find her money? I felt so sorry for her. Ruby write me soon.&lt;br&gt;
Freeda C.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
